00:40:24.090 --> 00:40:26.560
It's at the end of the day governed

00:40:27.690 --> 00:40:29.970
entirely and ultimately
by the physical laws.

00:40:29.970 --> 00:40:34.110
And so there's a mystery
as to explaining how,

00:40:34.110 --> 00:40:35.310
in terms of the laws of physics,

00:40:35.310 --> 00:40:38.730
you know, we can make certain
inferences about the system,

00:40:38.730 --> 00:40:39.633
but not others.

00:40:41.100 --> 00:40:44.130
So yeah, very large scale
assumptions in place here.

00:40:44.130 --> 00:40:48.153
The second one, I mean,
not sure what to say here.

00:40:49.440 --> 00:40:51.840
One thing, you know, this
is a specific example,

00:40:51.840 --> 00:40:54.090
and of course there's gonna
be very specific things

00:40:54.090 --> 00:40:57.900
to say about why plaques
are reliable and so on.

00:40:57.900 --> 00:41:01.800
But the point here is to try to tell

00:41:01.800 --> 00:41:04.410
a much more abstract and general story,

00:41:04.410 --> 00:41:07.233
and you know, to put it
in those abstract terms.

00:41:09.780 --> 00:41:11.550
We find very strong correlations

00:41:11.550 --> 00:41:15.810
between things in the present
and things in the past.

00:41:15.810 --> 00:41:17.460
We find few correlations

00:41:17.460 --> 00:41:19.800
between things in the present
and things in the future.

00:41:19.800 --> 00:41:22.533
And we qualify that in all
sorts of ways, and so on.

00:41:25.204 --> 00:41:26.610
And it is, you know, the
physics of our world,

00:41:26.610 --> 00:41:29.598
it seems to prevent the
correlations anyway,

00:41:29.598 --> 00:41:30.698
in whatever direction.

00:41:33.272 --> 00:41:34.105
The thought is, you know,

00:41:34.105 --> 00:41:35.040
it's the causal structure of the world

00:41:35.040 --> 00:41:37.530
that explains the solution.

00:41:37.530 --> 00:41:39.030
Then after that, you know,

00:41:39.030 --> 00:41:41.460
if you want to explain why are plaques

00:41:41.460 --> 00:41:43.980
specifically very strongly correlated

00:41:43.980 --> 00:41:45.390
with the events they report,

00:41:45.390 --> 00:41:47.190
well again, it's gonna be a local story

00:41:47.190 --> 00:41:50.310
about human practices and you know,

00:41:50.310 --> 00:41:52.470
why the people who
commissioned the plaques,

00:41:52.470 --> 00:41:56.073
they have an interest in
having reliable ones and so on.

00:41:56.970 --> 00:42:01.170
But the point is to have this
sort of much more abstract,

00:42:01.170 --> 00:42:04.110
much more general story on the table.

00:42:04.110 --> 00:42:05.917
- [Priya] (indistinct) and then.

00:42:05.917 --> 00:42:08.610
- [Audience] Yeah, thanks
so much for your talk.

00:42:08.610 --> 00:42:11.250
So, I'm totally on board

00:42:11.250 --> 00:42:13.350
with understanding the causal asymmetry

00:42:13.350 --> 00:42:16.020
in terms of this probabilistic asymmetry.

00:42:16.020 --> 00:42:20.430
And I was curious whether you
see as part of your project,

00:42:20.430 --> 00:42:21.810
as trying to say something

00:42:21.810 --> 00:42:24.870
about why those
asymmetries get manifested,

00:42:24.870 --> 00:42:26.580
given the way the universe is.

00:42:26.580 --> 00:42:27.900
So, even given everything you've said,

00:42:27.900 --> 00:42:30.063
if you did not have independent causes,

00:42:30.900 --> 00:42:35.430
then you know, it would
trivially be true, but unhelpful.

00:42:35.430 --> 00:42:36.420
Causal marker would apply.

00:42:36.420 --> 00:42:38.070
You couldn't use it for anything.

00:42:39.550 --> 00:42:40.383
And it seems to me,

00:42:40.383 --> 00:42:43.080
there are sort of ongoing
debates about this.

00:42:43.080 --> 00:42:44.760
So, I had taken the story

00:42:44.760 --> 00:42:46.080
as someone like Dan Hausman says,

00:42:46.080 --> 00:42:48.600
I mean he appeals basically
the same asymmetry,

00:42:48.600 --> 00:42:49.620
and he would say, you know,

00:42:49.620 --> 00:42:53.130
that there's no causation in
closed deterministic systems,

00:42:53.130 --> 00:42:54.450
so it's only when we coarse grain

00:42:54.450 --> 00:42:57.180
and consider sort of open subsystems.

00:42:57.180 --> 00:42:59.250
And it seemed to me that
orientation of your talk

00:42:59.250 --> 00:43:01.110
went in that direction.

00:43:01.110 --> 00:43:03.241
Mattias Frisch disagrees.

00:43:03.241 --> 00:43:06.510
So, I'm curious whether
this is part of your project

00:43:06.510 --> 00:43:08.550
to then say something about that.

00:43:08.550 --> 00:43:10.670
- Yeah, good, thanks. Thanks.

00:43:10.670 --> 00:43:14.810
I'm more on the side of
the causal asymmetry.

00:43:14.810 --> 00:43:18.093
It sort of emerges when you
are coarse graining the system,

00:43:19.590 --> 00:43:22.923
and you get probabilities, and so on.

00:43:27.000 --> 00:43:27.833
As you mentioned,

00:43:27.833 --> 00:43:30.871
this is something on which
people have had a lot say,

00:43:30.871 --> 00:43:33.090
and I don't have much more to add to this.

00:43:33.090 --> 00:43:35.580
This is sort of the
background. You're right.

00:43:35.580 --> 00:43:36.630
But I think, you know,

00:43:36.630 --> 00:43:38.370
if you think about the causal asymmetry

00:43:38.370 --> 00:43:39.570
in totally different terms,

00:43:39.570 --> 00:43:42.453
as this sort of fundamental
arrows there is in the world,

00:43:44.280 --> 00:43:47.280
perhaps people who have sort
of more robust metaphysics

00:43:47.280 --> 00:43:49.380
are inclined to think of it that way.

00:43:49.380 --> 00:43:51.633
You can also tell that story, I think.

00:43:53.721 --> 00:43:56.299
- [Priya] Last question.
Okay, we have two.

00:43:56.299 --> 00:43:58.775
Peter and (indistinct).

00:43:58.775 --> 00:44:01.902
- [Peter] So, I wonder what extent,

00:44:01.902 --> 00:44:03.199
really reflecting whatever-

00:44:03.199 --> 00:44:04.440
- [Speaker] Sorry, you have to-

00:44:04.440 --> 00:44:05.850
- [Peter] I was pressing
it, then I wasn't.

00:44:05.850 --> 00:44:07.260
- [Speaker] Yeah, you don't have to-

00:44:07.260 --> 00:44:08.670
- [Peter] Only press it once, right.

00:44:08.670 --> 00:44:11.163
Excuse me, I haven't
gathered that obviously.

00:44:14.970 --> 00:44:19.350
So, it feels as if the
history is very protected

00:44:19.350 --> 00:44:21.150
in the case of The Mayflower.

00:44:21.150 --> 00:44:23.940
It really takes an effort
of will over centuries

00:44:23.940 --> 00:44:26.130
for the plaque to exist.

00:44:26.130 --> 00:44:27.780
And if something is forgotten,

00:44:27.780 --> 00:44:30.450
then refinding it can be a huge effort.

00:44:30.450 --> 00:44:32.940
And if an effort of will is imposed

00:44:32.940 --> 00:44:35.220
to deliberately forget,

00:44:35.220 --> 00:44:38.820
so a criminal wants an
act not to be remembered,

00:44:38.820 --> 00:44:42.270
then the will to forget it

00:44:42.270 --> 00:44:44.850
becomes a very serious part
of whether it is remembered,

00:44:44.850 --> 00:44:47.103
whether it is a commemoration.

00:44:48.870 --> 00:44:52.530
So how would you see willpower, 

00:44:52.530 --> 00:44:56.910
just the will, the human
will, figuring into this?

00:44:56.910 --> 00:44:59.160
- That's interesting. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:44:59.160 --> 00:45:01.890
You're absolutely right
here that, you know,

00:45:02.880 --> 00:45:04.830
in this example there's a lot to say

00:45:04.830 --> 00:45:09.830
about human practices of
memorializing certain events

00:45:11.280 --> 00:45:12.113
and not others.

00:45:14.520 --> 00:45:16.020
Yeah.

00:45:16.020 --> 00:45:19.983
I don't have anything sort of
insightful to say about this.

00:45:22.860 --> 00:45:26.373
The idea is, you know, at a certain level,

00:45:27.240 --> 00:45:28.533
The Mayflower thing,

00:45:30.690 --> 00:45:32.760
you could use examples
that have nothing to do

00:45:32.760 --> 00:45:37.760
with human action and human
practices to tell the point.

00:45:38.760 --> 00:45:40.443
This falls all over there.

00:45:42.725 --> 00:45:46.053
You know, it's a sign of the
existence of the species,

00:45:47.541 --> 00:45:49.223
millions or billions of years ago.

00:45:51.083 --> 00:45:53.430
But physics tells me whether
that species really existed,

00:45:53.430 --> 00:45:57.510
it depends on not only the
existence of that fossil,

00:45:57.510 --> 00:46:00.000
but actually the entire cross-section

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:02.370
of the forward light cone, right?

00:46:02.370 --> 00:46:04.170
And of course there's perhaps not gonna be

00:46:04.170 --> 00:46:07.380
any other macroscopic
signs of the existence

00:46:07.380 --> 00:46:08.213
of that species.

00:46:08.213 --> 00:46:10.410
Maybe the fossil is the only
macroscopic record we have,

00:46:10.410 --> 00:46:14.220
but at the macroscopic levels, you know,

00:46:14.220 --> 00:46:18.033
there's still gonna be correlations,

00:46:19.440 --> 00:46:21.270
and as far as how is that possible?

00:46:21.270 --> 00:46:22.380
You know, how is it possible

00:46:22.380 --> 00:46:24.720
for the fossil to still
provide information

00:46:24.720 --> 00:46:25.923
if that's the case.

00:46:28.958 --> 00:46:30.291
- [Priya] Harry.

00:46:31.410 --> 00:46:33.570
- [Harry] Hey, thank you
for all the great talk.

00:46:33.570 --> 00:46:35.430
So what I want to ask is that,

00:46:35.430 --> 00:46:37.530
certainly at the Newtonian level,

00:46:37.530 --> 00:46:40.230
there is time reversal
symmetry in the laws,

00:46:40.230 --> 00:46:43.650
but at the quantum filter
theory level, would there be?

00:46:43.650 --> 00:46:45.510
Because CPT is preserved,

00:46:45.510 --> 00:46:48.780
and we know by matter
antimatter, CP is violated,

00:46:48.780 --> 00:46:50.970
so time reversal wouldn't hold

00:46:50.970 --> 00:46:53.610
at the quantum filter theory level.

00:46:53.610 --> 00:46:55.650
So maybe that leaves any perspective

00:46:55.650 --> 00:46:58.863
of how this asymmetry might arise?

00:47:00.030 --> 00:47:01.380
- This is a great question,

00:47:01.380 --> 00:47:04.971
and I have absolutely nothing to say.

00:47:04.971 --> 00:47:07.121
- [Harry] Actually,
the cosmologists might.

00:47:08.541 --> 00:47:12.210
- This is outside of my area

00:47:12.210 --> 00:47:16.863
of not complete incompetence, I guess.

00:47:18.777 --> 00:47:21.180
And I wish somebody who was knowledgeable

00:47:21.180 --> 00:47:25.710
about those issues would answer.

00:47:25.710 --> 00:47:28.263
I guess one thing to say is, you know,

00:47:31.700 --> 00:47:33.630
the sort of inferences we make,

00:47:34.500 --> 00:47:36.390
they're based on microscopic phenomena

00:47:36.390 --> 00:47:38.250
and at the microscopic level,

00:47:38.250 --> 00:47:40.020
I assume the dynamics is,

00:47:40.020 --> 00:47:42.603
it's kind of quasi deterministic, right?

00:47:43.590 --> 00:47:46.080
So I'm perhaps skeptical

00:47:46.080 --> 00:47:48.930
that going to the fundamental levels

00:47:48.930 --> 00:47:50.830
is going to sort of tell you

00:47:52.056 --> 00:47:53.613
or provide the answer here.

00:47:55.080 --> 00:47:56.280
Because again, you know,

00:47:57.510 --> 00:47:59.220
whatever asymmetry you're going to find,

00:47:59.220 --> 00:48:01.920
it doesn't really seem to percolate up.

00:48:01.920 --> 00:48:04.790
But again, you know, I don't
know much about those issues.

00:48:04.790 --> 00:48:06.937
- [Priya] I let (indistinct)
make a quick comment.

00:48:06.937 --> 00:48:09.337
- [Audience] I mean, I
can answer that question.

00:48:10.410 --> 00:48:12.720
You might worry, in quantum theory,

00:48:12.720 --> 00:48:14.790
if you've got a fundamental
collapse theory,

00:48:14.790 --> 00:48:16.800
a fundamentally indeterministic theory.

00:48:16.800 --> 00:48:20.010
Then you might be able to
predict and not retrodict.

00:48:20.010 --> 00:48:21.870
But CPT has nothing to do with it,

00:48:21.870 --> 00:48:26.870
because as long as you obey CPT,

00:48:27.510 --> 00:48:29.190
there's gonna be information preservation

00:48:29.190 --> 00:48:31.110
at the global scale in both directions.

00:48:31.110 --> 00:48:34.140
That's not gonna break.
That'll be perfectly symmetric.

00:48:34.140 --> 00:48:36.270
From perfect information at any time,

00:48:36.270 --> 00:48:38.280
you can get perfect
information at any other time.

00:48:38.280 --> 00:48:39.720
- [Audience] You can say that
information is not preserved

00:48:39.720 --> 00:48:41.296
in quantum theory.

00:48:41.296 --> 00:48:42.129
- Yeah, but the time reversal,

00:48:42.129 --> 00:48:43.500
you said the time reversal was broken,

00:48:43.500 --> 00:48:45.150
the relevant time reversal isn't.

00:48:45.990 --> 00:48:49.050
Relevant time reversal is the preservation

00:48:49.050 --> 00:48:50.750
of information in both directions.

00:48:51.840 --> 00:48:54.210
- [Priya] Great. Thanks
once again, Thomas.

